preConditionHook:
// SOMEWHERE IN THE LAST lookback BARS THERE WAS A RUN OF AT LEAST runBars
// CONSECUTIVE BULL TREND BARS -- earlier strength, not necessarily still in
// progress. Short is the mirror. Negate the placement for Brooks's "the rally
// never produced two consecutive strong bull trend bars".
//
// ONE RULE COVERS TWO SOURCES: "a strong bull trend bar occurred within the
// last K bars" is this at runBars = 1, and "the rally did not contain two
// consecutive strong bull trend bars" is this at runBars = 2, negated.
//
// NOT StrongTrendBarRun, which requires the run to END at the current bar:
// "strength ten bars ago" and "strength right now" fire on different bars. At
// lookback = runBars the two coincide; at the defaults they do not.
//
// NOT LargeTrendBarCountInWindow or TrendBarCountDominanceInWindow, which count
// qualifying bars anywhere in the window without requiring them to be adjacent.
//
// DROPPED, deliberately: one source also asked that the run's bars have a range
// at least the average range. ANDing BarRangeAboveAtrMultiple in a pane is NOT
// equivalent -- that tests the CURRENT bar, while the source's term is inside
// the scan -- so the stricter reading is noted here rather than coded.
//
// The bar shape is StrongTrendBarRun's settled definition: a strict body
// direction and a body of at least bodyFraction of the bar's own range. The
// inner all-of-N loops start true and let any failing bar clear the flag, and
// the outer scan runs to completion rather than breaking, so both loops run
// unconditionally and EasyLanguage's lack of short-circuiting cannot matter.
//
// When runBars > lookback the outer loop's upper bound is negative and the scan
// never runs, so the rule is simply false -- no guard needed.
//
// The flags are class members and persist across bars, so they are reset at the
// top of the hook and at the top of each scan step.
//
// Products, not quotients: EasyLanguage raises a runtime divide-by-zero and a
// zero-range bar is legal data.
//
// Deepest bar touched: lookback - 1.
foundUp = false;
foundDn = false;
for (ii = 0; ii <= (int)lookback - (int)runBars; ++ii) {
    runUpHere = true;
    runDnHere = true;
    for (jj = 0; jj <= (int)runBars - 1; ++jj) {
        if (el_le(close[ii + jj], open[ii + jj])) runUpHere = false;
        if (el_lt(close[ii + jj] - open[ii + jj], bodyFraction * (high[ii + jj] - low[ii + jj]))) runUpHere = false;
        if (el_ge(close[ii + jj], open[ii + jj])) runDnHere = false;
        if (el_lt(open[ii + jj] - close[ii + jj], bodyFraction * (high[ii + jj] - low[ii + jj]))) runDnHere = false;
    }
    if (runUpHere) foundUp = true;
    if (runDnHere) foundDn = true;
}
